WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.250
1.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.299
The sun radiates more energy in 15 minutes
than humans use every year around the world.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:20.510
If only we could find a way to channel the
sun's energy more efficiently.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.510
2.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.380
You can make electricity from anything.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.130
Light, wind, water and even animal manure.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:33.210
The most common way of producing electricity
around the world is by burning coal.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.210
3.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:39.850
In the early 1900s christmas lights were so
ridiculously expensive that they were often

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.210
rented instead of sold.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.320
If you had lights at christmas, it was a big
status symbol.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.320
4.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.020
A single bolt of lightening can contain up
to 3 million volts, that's enough electricity

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.700
to serve over 200,000 homes.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.470
Also lightening can be up to five times hotter
than the surface of the sun.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.470
5.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.710
Electricity is lazy, it will find the quickest
path to the ground.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:10.540
Did you know that electricity can "jump",
it can literally leap across a distance to

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.210
find the nearest source of earth.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.860
The higher the voltage the further it can
jump.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:20.090
This is why you have to be super careful around
live wires and power sockets.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.090
6.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.810
Your heart works on electricity.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:27.229
Muscle cells in the heart are contracted by
electricity that passes through it.

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:35.990
Electrocardiogram or ECG machines, AKA heart
rate monitors, used in hospitals work by measuring

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.479
how much electricity is going through the
patients heart.

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:43.350
This causes the erratic movements of the line
you see on screen.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.420
7.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.380
Electricity can be used to create the world's
most powerful magnets, commonly known as electromagnets.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.380
8.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:55.789
Iceland was the first ever country to produce
all of its electricity from renewable sources.

00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:56.789
Go Iceland!

00:01:56.789 --> 00:01:57.789
9.

00:01:57.789 --> 00:02:03.049
Electricity travels at the speed of light,
that's more than 186,000 miles every second.

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:04.049
10.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:06.149
But what actually is electricity?

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:12.000
It's the flow of charged particles, electrons
and protons, around a closed circuit.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:22.230
Electricity cannot flow if a circuit is not
a complete loop.

